:: Robin Breakup
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>

"We... we need to talk," you say. Robin looks up at you, then stiffens when <<he>> hears your tone. <<He>> waits for you to continue.
<br><br>

<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You struggle to meet <<his>> eyes. "I-I don't think I can keep doing this. Could we... go back to being friends?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"I-I... We... Can we go back to being friends?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You keep your voice low. "I-I... We... Can we go back to being friends? I think that would be better."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I'm sorry, Robin. I don't think this is working for me," you say. "Could we go back to being friends?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Robin, I think we should break up," you say. "I still want us to be friends."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"I don't think this works for me. I want to go back to being friends."
<<else>>
	"We... we should break up. Let's just be friends again."
<</if>>
<br><br>

"W-what!? Wha... was it something I did wrong?" Robin's eyes widen, and <<he>> leans towards you before stopping <<himself>>. "I'm sorry! I can fix it! I promise!" You lean forward and hug <<him>>, holding <<him>> close while <<he>> tries to catch up with what you just said.
