Robin grips the back of your clothes and cries against you. You run your fingers through <<his>> hair, staying with <<him>> until <<his>> hold slowly loosens. When you finally pull away, <<he>> reaches after you, then lets <<his>> hand fall back into <<his>> lap. You stop by the door, but there is little else you can say without making things harder. Robin is going to need some space to process this.
